; The lift cage of the v2 third section (assets/art/v2/level0_r2/level0_section3_exit_r2.svg). The
; area is the trip wire of the ambush, not a wall: it covers the last stretch of floor before the
; cage — world x 3040…3440 across the whole walk band (y 300…600) — with the section placed at
; level x 2560 (WorldScale 1280/680, OffsetY -227.06). That is the 240 px of floor in front of the
; painted cage opening (mockup x 382…602, y 100…280 = world x 3279.1…3693.6, y -38.8…300.0), so the
; grate goes and the guards come out as the hero gets near the cage, not the moment he steps into
; the section (world x 2560…3840); spanning the full depth of the band leaves no way to sneak past
; along its far or near edge. Place this node at world (3240, 450).
; The root is an Area2D that blocks nothing: layer 0, mask 2 (the Player layer), monitoring.
; The level fills in Caged, Exits, Gate, Player and Director; the two caged guards stand with their
; feet at world (3399.5, 315.1) and (3584.0, 315.1) and walk out to their Exits markers, which
; belong inside the band. tests/smoke/props_guard_cage.gd rebuilds all of it from these numbers.
